CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^.*implicit arithmetic conversion not permitted.*$
--
Verifies that a class operand with a single arithmetic-typed
user-defined conversion operator is converted via that operator
when used with a built-in binary arithmetic operator and an
arithmetic operand.

Per [over.match.oper]/9 + [over.built]: when no operator overload
is selected, the operator is treated as built-in, and operands
are subject to user-defined conversion sequences to the built-in
operator's parameter types.

Without the fix, the struct operand reaches the C-style
arithmetic typecheck unchanged and surfaces the spurious
"implicit arithmetic conversion not permitted" diagnostic on both
lvalue (named local) and rvalue (function return) operands.
